/T (A key conclusion is that exception handling and memory management are connected. During stack unwinding, automatic objects are destroyed. RAII, standard containers, and smart pointers use this behaviour to release resources reliably. Modern C++ design should therefore prefer automatic resource management over scattered manual cleanup.)
/E (A key conclusion is that exception handling and memory management are connected. During stack unwinding, automatic objects are destroyed. RAII, standard containers, and smart pointers use this behaviour to release resources reliably. Modern C++ design should therefore prefer automatic resource management over scattered manual cleanup.)
