/Title (A handler must match the exception type. More specific handlers should normally appear before broader handlers. If a function does not handle an exception locally, it can propagate to its caller. C++ searches outward for a matching handler; during this process, local automatic objects are destroyed. This is known as stack unwinding. If no matching handler is found, the program calls std::terminate.)
